WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.540
A covered financial institution must develop, implement, and maintain a written information security program.

2
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:15.240
The program must be appropriate to the institution's size and complexity, the nature and scope of its activities, and the sensitivity of customer information.

3
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:21.020
Proportionality affects implementation; safeguards must still reflect actual risk.

4
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:26.500
The institution must designate a Qualified Individual to implement and supervise the program.

5
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:30.520
The Rule does not prescribe a specific degree or job title.

6
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:33.580
Required capability depends on the environment.

7
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:38.640
The Qualified Individual may be an employee or may work for an affiliate or service provider.

8
00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:50.500
When that role is external, the institution must designate a senior member of its personnel to provide direction and oversight, and the affiliate or provider must maintain a protective information security program.

9
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.160
Outsourcing does not transfer accountability.

10
00:00:53.440 --> 00:01:00.560
The program must be based on a risk assessment of reasonably foreseeable internal and external risks to customer information.

11
00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:11.620
A sound assessment establishes what information exists, where it moves, who can reach it, and which data, personnel, devices, systems, and facilities support it.

12
00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:19.560
Address unauthorized disclosure, misuse, alteration, destruction, disruption, and other compromise.

13
00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:38.080
For institutions subject to the written-assessment requirements, the assessment must document criteria for evaluating and categorizing risks, criteria for assessing confidentiality, integrity, availability, and existing controls, and requirements describing how risks will be mitigated or accepted.

14
00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:46.420
A list of vulnerabilities without evaluation, control analysis, and treatment decisions is not necessarily a complete risk assessment.

15
00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:48.780
Risk assessment is cyclical.

16
00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:59.760
Reassess when operations, systems, threats, personnel, or business arrangements change, and periodically even when no single change appears decisive.

17
00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:08.500
Preserve the evidence connecting identified risks to control decisions, accepted exposure, responsible owners, and review dates.

18
00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:14.600
That traceability makes the written program an operating management system rather than a static policy binder.
